"hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1243,"Maymun (ibn Mahran) said, ""I asked Nafi', 'Did Ibn 'Umar ever
invite people to a banquet?' He said, 'A camel of his once broke something
and so we sacrificed it. Then Ibn 'Umar said, ""Gather the people of Madina
for me."" I said, ""Abu 'Abdu'r-Rahman, for what? We do not have any bread.""
He said, ""O Allah, praise belongs to You. These are bits of meat and this
is broth,"" or he said, ""Broth and meat chunks. Whoever wishes can eat and
whoever wishes can leave it.""'"""
1244,"Sa'ib ibn Yazid, may Allah have mercy on him, reported that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Some men from the Quraysh used to stand at the door of Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, to learn something from him. When the shadow shifted, he would say, 'Get up, for whatever remains of the day is for Shaytan,' and then he would pass by them and make them get up firmly."" While they were like that, they were told, ""This is a young man from Banu Hashish who composes poetry."" They called him and said, ""What poetry have you composed?"" He said, ""If you have set out on a journey this morning, then leave Salim alone, for old age and the religion of Islam are sufficient to keep a person from evil."" Umar said, ""That is enough for you. You have spoken the truth, you have spoken the truth."""
1245,"As-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, may Allah have mercy on him, said, ""Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to pass by us close to midday and say, 'Get up and take a nap, for whatever remains of the day belongs to Shaytan.'"""
"1246","Sayyiduna Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he would perform the Friday prayer and then take a siqaylah (afternoon nap)."
1247,"Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said, ""When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the wine that the people of Madina had was made from unripe dates and dried dates. One day I was serving the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, in the house of Abu Talha, may Allah be pleased with him, when a man passed by and said, 'Wine has been prohibited.' He did not ask when it had been prohibited nor look into the matter further, but said, 'Anas, pour out this wine.' Then it was mentioned in the house of Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, until the heat of the sun had died down, and he bathed. Umm Sulaym then perfumed him, and he went to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and told him what had happened, just as the man had described it.""

Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said, ""He never put wine to his lips again after that."""
1248,"Khawwat ibn Jubayr, may Allah have mercy on him, said, ""Sleeping at the beginning of the day is ignorance, sleeping in the middle of it is the Sunna, and sleeping at the end of it is stupidity."""
